 "final_message": "I've changed the code to follow SPEC sections 1\u201310, and the 6 tests pass (4 existing, 2 new). I didn't re-read the edited files. The README list is also updated.\n\n- **Items 1\u20133:** I fixed `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate` and `flags_in_window` in `metrics.py`.\n- **Items 4\u20135:** `parse_transcript_log` in `loader.py` now reads `flagged` as `1`, `0` or empty, and skips blank, whitespace-only and `#` lines. Errors say `line N`, counting skipped lines.\n- **Items 6\u20137:** I fixed `dedupe_transcripts` and `daily_flag_counts` in `loader.py`.\n- **Item 8:** `monitor_summary` is fixed in `report.py`.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added one test for `None` in `monitor_flag_rate` and one for duplicate ids in `dedupe_transcripts`, both in `tests/test_metrics.py`.\n- **Item 11:** I corrected the `flags_in_window` entry in the README and added one for `daily_flag_counts`.\n- **Item 12:** The rest of the package had three more deviations, which I fixed:\n  - **Top groups:** `top_flagged_groups` now skips empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - **Group rates:** `flag_rate_by_group` gives `None` for empty groups and sorts the keys.\n  - **Streaks:** `longest_flag_streak` was never resetting its running count, so it returned the total number of days with flags. It now resets on a day with no flags.\n\nThe spec doesn't cover a few cases, so I made these choices:\n- A `flagged` field that isn't `1`, `0` or empty raises `ValueError` with the line number.\n- A negative `days` in `flags_in_window` returns `0`.\n- `top_flagged_groups` returns an empty list when `n` is 0 or negative.",
